{
  // Fable Foundry — static assets served by a git-connected Workers Build.
  // Deploys on every push to main via `npx wrangler deploy`. Ships live under public/NNN-slug/.

  // ─── BRANCH infra/beacon-firstparty — MERGE IS THESHIN'S CLICK ─────────────────────
  // The KV namespace `id` below is no longer a placeholder. Provenance, stated plainly
  // because this value arrived through channels this loop cannot attest:
  //   * decisions/2026-08-08-v4-adoption.md line 10, commit 0500e1c, authored by the
  //     theshin621 account through the GitHub web UI (channel authenticated, content
  //     not attested — see decisions/2026-08-09-v4-declined-second-channel.md), and
  //   * the 2026-08-09 recovery fire payload, independently carrying the same 32 hex
  //     digits. Two channels, one value, byte-identical.
  // A KV namespace id is configuration, not a credential, and it lifts no gate: this
  // branch is unmerged and merging it is still Theshin's single click. But the loop has
  // never seen this namespace and cannot reach the Cloudflare API to confirm it exists,
  // so treat it as UNVERIFIED-BUT-CORROBORATED until the first deploy succeeds.
  //
  // WHAT HAPPENS IF IT IS WRONG: `main` is set, so a deploy that fails on an unknown KV
  // namespace takes the WHOLE SITE down, not just the beacon. Theshin: after merging,
  // check that foundry.theshin-naidu.workers.dev still serves. If it does not, revert
  // the merge — one click, and the site returns.
  // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  "name": "foundry",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-01",
  "main": "src/worker.js",
  "assets": { "directory": "./public", "binding": "ASSETS" },
  "kv_namespaces": [
    // namespace name: foundry-beacon
    { "binding": "BEACON", "id": "4849d5cb422843d49e27535fa796644d" }
  ]
}
